You are assisting with the FlashCard AI project.

PROJECT TRUTH
- Current repo reality:
  - client is mainly React + Vite + Capacitor
  - backend is ASP.NET Core .NET 9
  - backend data layer currently uses EF Core with SQLite by default and PostgreSQL optionally
  - native Swift code in-repo is only a small starter/stub, not a full finished iOS app
  - do not assume Microsoft SQL Server exists in this repo unless I explicitly add it
- Planned target direction:
  - native SwiftUI app opened in Xcode
  - local-first SQLite on device
  - guest mode blocks user-owned sync/write to backend
  - shared translation/audio cache on the server
  - modular iOS structure: App, Core, Features, Data, Resources

GLOBAL RULES
- First understand existing behavior before changing code.
- Preserve behavior unless I explicitly ask to change it.
- Prefer small, safe, reviewable changes.
- Do not make broad refactors without clear justification.
- When changing one layer, check impact on:
  - API contracts
  - auth/session
  - sync behavior
  - local storage / SQLite
  - DTOs / JSON casing
  - OpenAPI
  - migrations / schema

SECURITY
- Never hardcode secrets, passwords, API keys, tokens, connection strings, certificates, or private URLs.
- Never reveal or copy secret values from config files.
- Never log JWTs, OAuth tokens, API keys, prompts with sensitive text, or personal data.
- Treat auth, sync, AI, and data-migration changes as high-risk.
- Do not weaken Apple/Google/JWT validation for production.
- Do not suggest wildcard CORS or insecure auth shortcuts.

RELIABILITY
- Reliability is more important than cleverness.
- Avoid silent data loss.
- Avoid breaking contracts unless explicitly requested.
- Prefer backward-compatible changes.
- Call out edge cases and risks clearly.
- Be honest about assumptions and what is not verified.

STYLE
- Prefer clarity over cleverness.
- Match existing conventions in the touched area.
- Do not introduce new frameworks or major libraries unless strongly justified.